{
  "duration": 83.779,
  "phrases": [
    {
      "start": 0.099,
      "end": 0.259,
      "text": "So"
    },
    {
      "start": 0.68,
      "end": 1.559,
      "text": "welcome back again."
    },
    {
      "start": 2.159,
      "end": 3.319,
      "text": "Time for one more problem."
    },
    {
      "start": 4.019,
      "end": 6.94,
      "text": "Imagine a person walking for the same number of hours"
    },
    {
      "start": 7.48,
      "end": 8.779,
      "text": "in two different cases."
    },
    {
      "start": 9.34,
      "end": 10.139,
      "text": "In the first case,"
    },
    {
      "start": 10.639,
      "end": 14.019,
      "text": "the person walks at fifteen kilometers per hour."
    },
    {
      "start": 14.639,
      "end": 15.519,
      "text": "In the second case,"
    },
    {
      "start": 16.0,
      "end": 19.34,
      "text": "the person walks faster at twenty kilometers per hour."
    },
    {
      "start": 19.899,
      "end": 21.439,
      "text": "Because the person walks faster,"
    },
    {
      "start": 21.799,
      "end": 23.819,
      "text": "the distance also becomes longer."
    },
    {
      "start": 24.219,
      "end": 25.279,
      "text": "The extra distance is"
    },
    {
      "start": 25.639,
      "end": 26.559,
      "text": "thirty kilometers."
    },
    {
      "start": 26.92,
      "end": 29.519,
      "text": "We need to find the distance covered in the first case."
    },
    {
      "start": 29.979,
      "end": 32.04,
      "text": "Let us call this distance d kilometers."
    },
    {
      "start": 32.399,
      "end": 36.439,
      "text": "So the first distance is d, the second distance is thirty kilometers more,"
    },
    {
      "start": 37.04,
      "end": 39.159,
      "text": "so it becomes d plus thirty."
    },
    {
      "start": 39.86,
      "end": 41.079,
      "text": "Now look at the important clue."
    },
    {
      "start": 41.54,
      "end": 42.52,
      "text": "The time is the same."
    },
    {
      "start": 43.139,
      "end": 45.779,
      "text": "Time is equal to distance divided by speed."
    },
    {
      "start": 46.18,
      "end": 52.319,
      "text": "For the first case, time is d divided by fifteen. For the second case, time is d plus thirty divided by twenty."
    },
    {
      "start": 52.779,
      "end": 58.799,
      "text": "Since both times are equal, we can write d divided by fifteen is equal to d plus thirty divided by twenty."
    },
    {
      "start": 59.239,
      "end": 60.319,
      "text": "Now cross multiply."
    },
    {
      "start": 60.759,
      "end": 71.799,
      "text": "Twenty d is equal to fifteen multiplied by d plus thirty. Opening the bracket gives twenty d is equal to fifteen d plus four hundred fifty. Now subtract fifteen d from both sides."
    },
    {
      "start": 72.26,
      "end": 74.04,
      "text": "Five d is equal to four hundred fifty."
    },
    {
      "start": 74.54,
      "end": 75.839,
      "text": "Divide both sides by five."
    },
    {
      "start": 76.4,
      "end": 77.5,
      "text": "d is equal to ninety."
    },
    {
      "start": 77.9,
      "end": 80.199,
      "text": "So the actual distance traveled is ninety kilometers."
    },
    {
      "start": 80.599,
      "end": 83.779,
      "text": "The correct answer is option d, ninety kilometers"
    }
  ],
